{"nodes": [{"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_advanced_topics", "label": "Advanced googletest Topics", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_assertionresult", "label": "testing::AssertionResult", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Returning AssertionResult instead of bool from a predicate lets EXPECT_TRUE print why the check failed, avoiding the arity-per-macro awkwardness of EXPECT_PRED*; supplying a success message too costs time in the passing path but makes EXPECT_FALSE informative."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_predicate_assertions", "label": "Predicate assertions (EXPECT_PRED*)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exists because the assertion set can never be complete; wrapping an existing bool function gets the argument values printed for free instead of hand-streaming a failure message into EXPECT_TRUE, which is awkward when the expression is expensive or has side effects."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_predicate_formatter", "label": "Predicate-formatter assertions (EXPECT_PRED_FORMAT*)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Full control over message formatting, and the only option when an argument cannot be streamed to ostream; FloatLE/DoubleLE ship as predicate-formats rather than new macros to avoid a macro explosion."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_staticasserttypeeq", "label": "StaticAssertTypeEq<T1, T2>", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Compile-time type equality check; inside a class or function template it only fires when the enclosing function is actually instantiated."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_assertion_placement", "label": "Assertion placement in void-returning functions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fatal assertions expand to a bare return, so they only compile in void functions - a direct consequence of Google not using exceptions. Constructors and destructors do not count as void-returning, and a fatal assertion in a helper called from one silently returns early, leaving a half-constructed object; use abort or SetUp/TearDown instead."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_gtest_skip", "label": "GTEST_SKIP()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lets a test bail out meaningfully when a runtime precondition of the system under test is not met, rather than failing or silently passing; usable in a fixture or Environment SetUp to skip a whole group."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_value_printer", "label": "Extensible value printer (operator<< / PrintTo)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Falls back to dumping raw bytes for unknown types, so users teach it their type. PrintTo exists as an alternative for teams that will not add operator<< or whose operator<< already means something else, and PrintTo wins when both are defined so test output can be customized without touching production formatting. Both must live in the same namespace as the type because of ADL."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_death_tests", "label": "Death tests", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Consistency checks that kill the process must themselves be tested, since a wrong check lets a corrupted program run on into memory corruption or security holes. A thrown exception is not death, because the caller could catch it. Statements run in a child process, so in-memory side effects (including frees) are invisible to the parent, which breaks heap checkers."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_death_test_styles", "label": "Death test styles (fast vs threadsafe)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The threadsafe style trades potentially dramatic execution-time increases for safety when forking in a multithreaded process; clone() is preferred over fork() on Linux because fork() more often hangs the child when the parent has threads. Deadlock via pthread_atfork handlers remains possible either way."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_death_test_naming", "label": "*DeathTest suite naming convention", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Suites whose name ends in DeathTest run before all other suites, so death tests execute while the process is still single-threaded. A fixture shared by both kinds is aliased with using/typedef rather than duplicated."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_regex_syntax", "label": "Death test regular expression syntax", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three dialects: RE2 when built with Bazel and Abseil, POSIX extended on Linux/Cygwin/Mac, and a hand-rolled minimal engine on Windows lacking alternation, grouping, brackets and repetition counts. GTEST_USES_SIMPLE_RE / GTEST_USES_POSIX_RE let portable tests branch."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_scoped_trace", "label": "SCOPED_TRACE / ScopedTrace", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Identifies which call site of a shared subroutine produced a failure without cluttering every assertion with a custom message; the ScopedTrace form takes explicit file and line so test helpers can attribute failures to their caller. Nested traces are reported in reverse order of encounter."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_propagating_fatal_failures", "label": "Propagating fatal failures from sub-routines", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ASSERT_* aborts only the current function, not the test, so a caller keeps running after a failed subroutine and can segfault. Three remedies: a listener that rethrows kFatalFailure as an exception, ASSERT_NO_FATAL_FAILURE, or checking HasFatalFailure(). Only failures on the asserting thread are counted."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_hasfatalfailure", "label": "HasFatalFailure() / HasNonfatalFailure()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_recordproperty", "label": "RecordProperty()", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Emits the last value per key as an XML attribute, so the key must be a valid XML attribute name and must not collide with name/status/time/classname/type_param/value_param. Where it is called decides which XML element it lands on: the test, the suite, or the top level."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_setuptestsuite", "label": "SetUpTestSuite / TearDownTestSuite", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A fresh fixture per test keeps tests independent and debuggable, but is prohibitively expensive for costly resources, so per-suite set-up shares one copy. Safe only if tests do not mutate the shared state or restore it, since test order is undefined; may run more than once when the fixture has derived classes, and must be public to be used with TEST_P."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_environment", "label": "testing::Environment global set-up/tear-down", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SetUp runs in registration order and TearDown in reverse, and TearDown always runs even when tests were skipped. Registration via a global variable is discouraged because cross-translation-unit initialization order is unspecified; write your own main() instead. googletest owns the registered objects."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_value_parameterized_tests", "label": "Value-parameterized tests", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Run one test body over many inputs without copying it - useful for flag combinations, several implementations of one interface, and data-driven testing, which the docs warn is easy to abuse."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_instantiate_test_suite_p", "label": "INSTANTIATE_TEST_SUITE_P", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Instantiates every TEST_P in the suite regardless of definition order, prefixing the instantiation name so a pattern can be instantiated repeatedly. Generators are evaluated lazily at InitGoogleTest time so they can depend on parsed flags. An uninstantiated TEST_P fails under GoogleTestVerification unless the suite is tagged GTEST_ALLOW_UNINSTANTIATED_PARAMETERIZED_TEST."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_abstract_tests", "label": "Value-parameterized abstract tests", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fixture declared in a header and TEST_P bodies in a .cc, so an interface author ships a conformance suite that each implementer instantiates for free, possibly many times in different files."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_param_name_generator", "label": "Custom parameter name generators", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PrintToStringParamName does not work for std::string or C strings, so a functor is needed; generated names must be non-empty, unique, ASCII alphanumeric, and free of underscores."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_typed_tests", "label": "Typed tests", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Repeat one test body over a known type list so m tests over n types do not become m*n hand-written TESTs; the type list must be aliased with using/typedef or the commas are parsed as extra macro arguments."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_type_parameterized_tests", "label": "Type-parameterized tests", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Like typed tests but the type list is supplied later, so an interface author can publish a conformance suite that each implementation instantiates with its own type; requires REGISTER_TYPED_TEST_SUITE_P to name every test before instantiation."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_testing_private_code", "label": "Testing private code (FRIEND_TEST, foo::internal, Pimpl)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Black-box testing through public interfaces is preferred, and a need to test internals usually signals a class doing too much. If unavoidable, move code to a foo::internal namespace with a *-internal.h header, refactor behind Pimpl, or declare the fixture or an individual test a friend; friendship does not extend to subclasses, so tests are not automatically friends of the class their fixture befriends."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_gtest_spi", "label": "gtest-spi.h EXPECT_FATAL_FAILURE / EXPECT_NONFATAL_FAILURE", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exists because googletest reports failures without exceptions, so a utility built on googletest cannot catch-and-assert; the statement cannot reference local non-static variables or members of this, and cannot return a value."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_registertest", "label": "testing::RegisterTest", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An advanced escape hatch for runtime test registration; the TEST macros are preferred because they hide the complexity of calling it."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_current_test_info", "label": "UnitTest::current_test_info()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Returns null when no test is running, so the suite name is unavailable inside SetUpTestSuite/TearDownTestSuite where it is already known implicitly."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_event_listener_api", "label": "Event listener API", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "EmptyTestEventListener exists so a subclass overrides only the events it cares about. On*Start events fire in list order and On*End in reverse so later listeners' output is framed by earlier ones; the default printer must be Released and deleted to suppress it. Listeners handling OnTestPartResult must not raise failures (infinite recursion) and must be ordered before failure-raising listeners so attribution is correct."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_sharding", "label": "Test sharding protocol", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GTEST_TOTAL_SHARDS and GTEST_SHARD_INDEX let the same binary run a disjoint subset on each machine, each test exactly once across shards. GTEST_SHARD_STATUS_FILE is a capability handshake: a sharding-aware binary creates the file, so a runner can tell which of its tests understand the protocol. The distribution across shards is explicitly not guaranteed."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_premature_exit_file", "label": "Premature-exit-file protocol", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The binary creates a file at start and deletes it when all work finishes, so a surviving file tells the runner the program exited unexpectedly; only active when TEST_PREMATURE_EXIT_FILE is set."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_catch_exceptions", "label": "Catching test-thrown exceptions (GTEST_CATCH_EXCEPTIONS)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Catching by default maximizes coverage of a run and prevents Windows pop-up dialogs that would block automation; disabling it hands the exception to the debugger so the call stack survives."}, {"id": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_sanitizer_integration", "label": "Sanitizer integration (weak on-report hooks)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "UBSan, ASan and TSan expose weak __*_on_report/__asan_on_error symbols; overriding them with FAIL() turns a sanitizer finding into an attributable test failure instead of a bare process-level report."}], "edges": [{"source": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_advanced_topics", "target": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_death_tests", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_advanced_topics", "target": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_value_parameterized_tests", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_advanced_topics", "target": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_typed_tests", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/chrono_thirdparty/yaml-cpp/test/googletest-1.13.0/docs/advanced.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_advanced_topics", "target": "src_chrono_thirdparty_yaml_cpp_test_googletest_1_13_0_docs_advanced_event_listener_api", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0,